The admission process for postgraduate (PG) programs at IIT Jodhpur involves several key steps and categories, as outlined in the available information: ### **General Categories of Admission** Candidates can apply under the following categories (applicability varies by program): - Full-time regular - Full-time sponsored - Part-time - External - Executive Programs may also combine modes (e.g., fully sponsored part-time). ### **Admission Process** 1. **Initial Shortlisting**: - Based on a composite score calculated from parameters like CAT Overall Scaled Score and Work Experience (Full Time). - Relaxations for reserved categories (SC/ST/PD) are applied as per Ministry of Education norms. 2. **Final Shortlisting**: - Candidates shortlisted based on the composite score are called for a **Personal Interview (virtual mode)**. - The final shortlist is determined using weighted criteria, though specific weights are not detailed in the retrieved context. 3. **Document Submission**: - Provisionally admitted students must submit copies of mark sheets, provisional certificates, and other required documents by the deadline specified in the Academic Calendar. - Failure to submit documents or provide false information may result in cancellation of admission. ### **Special Cases** - **M.Sc. Programs**: Admissions occur via: - **Joint Admission Test for Master’s (JAM)** organized by IITs. - **Institute-conducted written tests/interviews** for candidates with a relevant bachelor’s degree. - **Special Schemes**: Admissions under schemes like Quality Improvement Programme (QIP) or for Defence Personnel follow approved procedures by the Senate. ### **Eligibility Notes** - Minimum eligibility criteria are specified, but CETE (Center for Excellence in Teaching and Education) may impose higher standards if applications exceed available seats. - SC/ST/PD candidates receive relaxations in qualifying degree marks as per Ministry rules. ### **Additional Information** - Applicants shortlisted must bring their signed application form and educational testimonials at the time of admission. - For queries, contact the Office of Automation (oaautomation@iitj.ac.in) or the PhD Program Coordinator (pgcconvener@cete.iitj.ac.in). **Note**: The details provided are partially supported by the retrieved context. Specifics may vary depending on the program or category, and some criteria (e.g., exact weights for final shortlisting) are not fully detailed.

